Below is the change description:
The original implementation of native structured output support was too restrictive because it only worked if the converter was explicitly a BeanOutputConverter. By adding getJsonSchema to the StructuredOutputConverter interface, the framework can now support native structured output for any custom converter that provides a schema. The change in ChatModelCallAdvisor and the response context handling ensures a more robust and flexible approach to managing mutable context and building request augmentations, improving maintainability and interoperability.
The changes introduce a default getJsonSchema method to the StructuredOutputConverter interface, allowing all converters to optionally provide a schema. Consequently, DefaultCallResponseSpec was updated to use this method to retrieve the JSON schema for native structured output support, instead of checking for a specific BeanOutputConverter type. Additionally, ChatModelCallAdvisor now uses a mutable HashMap for the response context and leverages the ChatClientRequest.mutate() method for better flexibility, while the unit tests were expanded to include native structured output tests using a custom converter.

